# use — not offered in a master's workshop without leave
#
# The smith's anvil in the Test Forge is his: a blacksmith with a hammer in hand is not offered USE on it
# until the smith has given the use of the workshop (ask_to_use_workshop). With `goal use` pinned and
# nothing to pin it to, the phase runs some other goal — which is the proof.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-mm blacksmithing --grant-item hammer --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Forge" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Anvil"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

allow-flag-miss --goal-only
expect-state workshops stations=Test_Anvil,Test_Forge_Hearth,Test_Workbench master=blacksmith authorized=no
strategy succeed
goal use
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-no-verb use
expect-no-outcome crafting_opened
quit
